---
name: write-tests
description: Write meaningful unit and API tests (behaviour-named, deterministic, covering edge and error paths) that raise coverage with real signal. Use when adding behaviour or when a coverage gate fails.
---

# Write tests that can fail

## Checklist for every behaviour
- Happy path
- Each validation rule (one test per rule)
- Boundaries: 0, 1, max, max+1, empty, whitespace, unicode
- Error paths: not found, conflict, dependency down
- Idempotency / repeated calls where relevant

## How
- Name by behaviour: `test_hello_uses_default_name_when_missing`.
- Arrange / Act / Assert, one reason to fail.
- Test through the public interface (HTTP client / component render), not private helpers.
- Fake only at the boundary (database, network, clock). Do not mock the unit under test.
- Assert on outcomes (status, body, rendered text), not on call counts.

## When coverage is below the floor
Look at the uncovered lines in the gate output. For each: is it reachable behaviour (write the test) or dead code (delete it)? Never lower the threshold or exclude files to get green.

## Verify the test is real
Temporarily break the code under test. The test must fail. Restore the code.

